WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.640
Current insurance costs far more than the crashes it covers, because we still sell the pool through agents. This is First Principles Daily, Episode 78. American spend a few hundred billion dollars a year on personal auto insurance. A typical full coverage policy now commonly lands well over a thousand dollars, and in many states closer to 2000. The expected cost of the crashes, the repairs, and the injury payments that policy is supposed to cover, sits substantially lower.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:39.200
That gap is not mystery physics. It is a mandatory pool still priced like a 19th century paper product, one six month term at a time.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:54.200
Commissions, ads, 50 state filings, and the claims process sit inside every declarations page, treated as weather rather than as design. Walk the machinery that still produces the price and the stack starts to look chosen.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:01:17.220
The modern personal auto policy is a descendant of a 19th century agency system, and a large share of it is still sold that way. Independent and captive agents explain coverages, shop a handful of carriers, and take a commission that industry figures commonly put in the low to mid teens as a percent of premium on new business, somewhat less on renewals.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:31.760
That arrangement was rational when comparing policies meant reading paper, and when a driver had no other way to find a solvent insurer. It is harder to justify once the actuarial work is a database query, and the premium is paid by card.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:44.740
Stacked on the agent is a 50 state regulatory machine. The McCarran Ferguson Act of 1945 left insurance primarily to the states, so a national carrier does not file one product.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:54.640
The carrier files rates and forms, minimum limits, and uninsured motorist rules in 50 plus jurisdictions, each with its own clock and its own objections.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:02:07.840
That compliance apparatus is not optional, and its cost lives inside the price you pay. Because almost every state makes liability coverage mandatory, insurers do not have to convince you that you need the product.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:15.420
Carriers have to convince you to buy theirs, which is why auto insurance is one of the heaviest advertising categories in the country.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:25.300
The Gecko and the Spokesperson are not decoration. Those mascots are the competitive battlefield, and the bill is paid by people who are legally required to buy.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:35.960
Six month terms, a long application, a credit-based insurance score, a territorial rate, a commission, a filing, these are how the product has always been made.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:47.960
Expense ratios in the neighborhood of a quarter of premium are treated as the cost of doing business. Combined ratios that hover near break even in hard years are taken as proof the price is already tight.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:56.660
Nobody wakes up thinking the design is the problem. People inside the industry wake up thinking about the next rate filing and the next adflate.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:03.020
Combined ratio tightness is a cost-plus story. The tools on this show ask a different question.

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:12.600
What is the raw expected loss floor? The magic wand question for car insurance is not what the paper costs because there is almost no paper left.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:19.620
The irreducible purchase is a statistical promise that if this car hurts someone or gets hurt, the pool will pay.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:32.260
Wave the wand and you know each driver's true expected loss. You pay every honest claim at the commodity cost of parts, labor, and medical care, and you hold only the surplus a real tail event requires.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:46.420
That combined figure is the floor. A typical insured car has only a modest chance of a collision claim in any given year and when the claim happens the repair bill is usually a few thousand dollars, not the size of the annual premium.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:58.280
Multiply a low frequency by a mid-four figure severity and the expected physical damage cost is already only a fraction of what a full coverage driver pays before liability is added.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:10.560
Liability is the swing factor. Medical bills, lost wages, and pain in suffering on at-fault crashes and it is also the line where process inflates the check farthest from the underlying injury.

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:18.800
Even after a realistic expected liability number, industry-wide figures still leave a large residual that is not the crash.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:30.580
Insures published loss ratios commonly live around two-thirds of premium, swinging higher when parts and medical inflation outrun filed rates and lower after a hard market.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:39.040
That published ratio is muddy because some of what gets labeled loss is the cost of handling the claim rather than the indemnity check.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:49.600
A cautious reading of statutory filings is that pure indemnity is perhaps something like six tenths of the premium plus or minus a noticeable amount by year and by line.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:53.520
Capital belongs next to that indemnity, not above it.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:05:03.560
A pool that must survive a nuclear verdict or a statewide hailstorm carries surplus and a few cents of each premium dollar is a fair allowance for that carrying cost.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:13.440
Add expected indemnity to that thin capital charge and the magic wand price lands, roughly at two thirds to three quarters of what drivers currently pay.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:18.600
Now divide. Take the finished premium as one dollar sitting on that floor.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:28.720
One divided by a floor near two thirds gives a homemade idiot index of about one and a half and in some years the same division climbs a little past two.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:37.940
This is not a laboratory measurement. A listener who picks a different loss ratio year will get a different number but the size of the answer will not flip.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:47.820
The obvious objection from inside the industry is that combined ratios already sit near 100% in hard years so there cannot be fat left to squeeze.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:52.700
That objection confuses a full cost plus stack with a physical floor.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:06:00.080
If you load commissions, ads, filings and adjustment into the definition of cost, of course the ratio looks tight.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:05.780
The same way a rocket looks fairly priced once every bracket is accepted as a machined forging.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:18.400
The idiot index is the tool that refuses that acceptance. A ratio of two is not a rocket engine scandal but a quiet one on a mandatory product attached to more than 200 million vehicles.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:27.540
Half a premium dollar times a few hundred billion is the prize. Walk the stack instead of the combined ratio and the extra dollar has names.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:41.780
The first pocket is distribution. Agent commissions in personal auto are widely reported in the low to mid teens as a percent of premium on new business and lower on renewals and the carrier still has its own sales overhead.

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:54.220
Direct writers spent decades proving that removing the agent cuts a real slice of load then spent a large share of the savings on television so customer acquisition costs simply put on the commissions close.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:07:01.380
The second pocket is the comparison mess that makes that acquisition expensive. A six month bundled quote,

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:08.120
loaded with discounts and filed differently in every state is not a unit price anyone shops the way they shop gasoline.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:19.480
That is why auto insurance stays among the loudest advertising categories in the country and why a meaningful fraction of a mandatory premium is the cost of being persuaded which logo to buy.

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:35.820
The third pocket is the filing machine 50 state rate and form regulation turns every new price endorsement and telematics discount into a legal project whose per policy cost looks small but whose industry wide cost is a permanent head count.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:44.020
The nastier effect is to freeze the product in the shape of a six month policy a prior approval statute already knows how to review.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:58.800
The fourth pocket is the process around the claim paying the body shop and the clinic is the product fighting over betterment rental days total loss valuation and bodily injury files with attorneys on both sides is the process.

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:08.880
Loss adjustment expense plus lawyer driven severity sit on top of indemnity even after you grant that some fraud investigation is genuinely irreducible.

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:22.560
The fifth pocket is analogical pricing territory credit based insurance score marital status education prior limits those are correlates rather than miles speed time of day or closing distance.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:32.720
The result is a pool that over charges the careful mile and under charges the sloppy one until the good risks shop and the carrier spend still more to replace them.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:44.560
The sensors that would let you price the mile already live in the car and in the phone so the expensive part is no longer measurement but permission regulation and the will to throw away the old factors.

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:53.200
Adverse selection is what you get when you price the proxy not a law of nature stack those layers and the index stops being abstract.

00:08:53.400 --> 00:09:03.900
The raw expected crash is steel glass labor and medicine and almost everything above it is a process designed when information was scarce and the agent was the computer.

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:12.200
An index near to on a mandatory product attached to more than 200 million vehicles is a quiet scandal with a large prize.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:22.340
What would a from scratch pool actually keep a redesign would not start by inventing a cleverer discount it would start by asking what has to exist at all.

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:40.900
First move take the commissioned conversation out of a standardized mandatory product coverage attaches at the vehicle at registration at the original equipment manufacturer or at a posted per mile meter and the driver is in the pool by default the way they are in the road system by default.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:56.480
For that to work you need a solvent rated balance sheet or a transparent residual mechanism for the tail a coverage contract simple enough that it does not require a translator and a regulator willing to accept a product that is not distributed by an appointed agent.

00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:03.020
The save is the commission plus a large share of the brand spend because there is much less left to choose.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:11.260
Second move throw away the analogical rating plan as the primary price and put the mile and the manner of the mile at the center.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:25.320
The car already knows how far it went how late how fast how hard it stopped phones know a version of the same thing what has to be true is default on data with a privacy bargain people will actually sign.

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:37.900
Enough participation that the program is not just a magnet for careful drivers and a filing regime that can accept an algorithm without demanding it be restated as a 1994 territory and credit table.

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:43.000
The save is the adverse selection tax and a chunk of the war for preferred names.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:49.800
Third move make physical damage claims look like a parts and labor invoice instead of a negotiation.

00:10:49.800 --> 00:11:02.000
Direct repair with transparent parts prices instant total loss when the numbers say so rental handled as a known unit cost that attacks loss adjustment expense on the metal side.

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:12.540
Bodily injury is honestly harder because the severity there is as much civil justice system as medicine what remains genuinely hard should be named out romance.

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:18.620
Insolvency law will still demand surplus fraud does not vanish because the app is prettier.

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:29.280
50 state statute is a political fact and the independent agent channel is organized enough to defend itself credit based scores and territory are genuinely predictive.

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:37.140
So discarding them before the driving signal is universal will raise prices for some sympathetic households and start a political fire.

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:43.200
A residual market for drivers whose physics are expensive will still exist and still need funding.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:56.680
People will resist being watched the price is not a world with no insurance companies it is a pool whose load looks like a thin capital charge and a cheap computer not like a television budget and a commission sales force.

00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:04.660
None of this requires a new law of probability only treating the agent the ad and the proxy score as design choices.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:12.160
The load on a car insurance premium is a map of every job that used to require a person and has not yet been retired.

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:24.380
When the thing being sold as an expected value that a processor can compute for free a commissioned agent between the pool and the driver is a left over from the years when the computer was a human being with a rate manual.

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:36.200
A legal mandate wrapped in an opaque six month quote will also reliably generate an advertising arms race because the customer cannot shop a unit price and must buy something.

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:45.920
The clean response is to hang the price on the unit that creates the risk the mile the car the registration until there is almost nothing left to brand.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:56.700
Neither of those moves requires a new law of probability they require treating the agent the ad and the analogical score as design choices rather than as the product.

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:09.800
The question worth carrying is who actually tries this as a system not as a discount an auto maker a state that is tired of filing theater a direct carrier willing to make per mile the whole rate plan.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:22.840
The first concrete signal would be simple to read a quote that begins from the car's own miles rather than a 40 question application and an expense ratio claim set aside that has fallen into the single digits.

